course: dictionary
lesson: 3397
title: What is an experiment?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An experiment is a careful test. You ask a question, make a guess called a prediction, test it, and watch what happens. «In an experiment, a small mustard-like plant made more defence chemicals after hearing a recording of caterpillars chewing» shows scientists testing an idea and seeing what happened.
explain: In a fair test you change only one thing, called the variable, and keep everything else the same. Then any change in the result comes from that one thing. Measure and record what you see, then decide what your results show. This decision is your conclusion.
explain: Experiment has another meaning too: trying new things to see what they are like. Artists experiment with colours, and cooks experiment with recipes. «A thought experiment is an imagined situation used to test ideas» means you test an idea in your head, not with equipment.
explain: Safety comes first. Only do experiments with a teacher or adult, and wear goggles if needed. Never mix household chemicals to experiment, because mixing some of them can be dangerous.
fact: An experiment is a test done carefully to find out something or to check an idea.
fact: A fair test changes one thing, the variable, and keeps everything else the same.
fact: «Experiment» can also mean trying new things to see what they are like, as in «experiment with colours».
fact: In one experiment, goldfish learned to push a lever for food and remembered the time of day when it worked.
fact: Experiments are done only with a teacher or adult, and never by mixing household chemicals.
exercise: In a fair test, what do you do with everything except the one thing you change? | Write it as the conclusion | Throw it away | Change it too | *Keep it the same
exercise: «Darwin and his son experimented on this with grass seedlings in the 1880s.» What does experimented mean here? | Planted a new garden | *Tested an idea carefully | Ate the seedlings | Drew pictures of plants
exercise: Which way of doing an experiment is safe? | Tasting the mixture to check it | Doing it alone in the dark | *Doing it with a teacher or adult, wearing goggles if needed | Mixing household chemicals at home to see what happens
test: Mia says, «Let's experiment with paint colours!» What does experiment mean in her sentence? | Do a fair test with a teacher | Measure the rain | Stop painting | *Try new things to see what they are like
test: Why is a thought experiment called an experiment? | *You test the idea in your head, not with equipment | You test it with a big machine | You copy a friend's test | You forget the idea
exam: Which sentence uses experiment as a noun for a test? | Please experiment with the paints before you start | *Franklin's kite experiment, reported in 1752, was a famous test of electric charge | We will experiment in the garden tomorrow | Let's experiment with new recipes this weekend
